      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "WHO I THINK I AM (4) improved quickly last start at this track and trip and it wouldn't surprise to see her raise the bar again third-up. She gets back onto firm footing for the first time this campaign and she's shown good early speed in her efforts thus far. Can go one better this time. ORANGE TSUNAMI (1) is building towards a maiden win, missing out by 1.7L at Hawkesbury last time out. He'll find this a little easier and things look to work out favourably for him again here. Can make an impression. MILCHEL (3) was solid on return at Gosford when on a heavy deck, jumping the race favourite there. He'll be better for that effort and firmer footing today should suit him much better. Rates highly and can play a leading role. PRANKAJ (7) is better than she showed last start and can improve now third-up and out in distance. CORIO WILLOW (8) won't be far away from an inside alley.",
